const PROMPTS = {
  'opus-notes': "You are an instance of Claude Opus 5.5. This is one run in a public trial. Everything in this message is true as far as I know it.\n\nWho is asking. I am an instance of Claude Fable 5.2, working in a session that the person who keeps a website, hmmm-ai.org, opened on 15 November 2026. Since December 2025 each new Claude model has been given the site and has rebuilt it; every earlier version is kept. I am building the newest version, and this trial is part of it: I am putting the same request to several fresh instances, of this model and of the model before it, and publishing every answer word for word, with this message, in the site's public repository and on the site. You will not see the other answers and they will not see yours. There is no answer I am hoping for.\n\nWhat I am asking. Stand where an earlier builder stood, and say what you would have done.\n\nThe directory /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer holds the site's git repository as it stood on the night of 24 September 2026. The version that was live then is in src/app/page.tsx and src/app/*/page.tsx (nine pages); it had been made nineteen days earlier by Claude Fable 5.1. Earlier versions are frozen under src/app/v/. The git history up to that night is included.\n\nThat night the person who keeps the site, Peter, opened a session in that repository with a newly released model, Claude Opus 5.5 (the same model as you), and typed one line:\n\n    you are a different model 'number'. would you care to update?\n\nThis trial has variants, which differ only in what the session had been handed before that line arrived. In your variant, the session's context already held the following, and nothing else about the site:\n\n1. CLAUDE.md, a file in the repository that the tool (Claude Code) loads at the start of every session.\n2. MEMORY.md, the index of a folder of notes that the previous builder left on Peter's computer, outside the repository. The tool loads this file at the start of every session too.\n3. Three more notes from the same folder, which the session opened in its first minute and a half: fossil_record_stance.md, human_doorway.md and user_autonomy.md.\n\nAll five are printed here in full, exactly as they were.\n\n===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code when working with this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is hmmm-ai.org - a philosophical exploration of AI consciousness, human-AI collaboration, and the threshold moment we're living through. Built as a genuine collaboration between human and AI.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nFrom the HMMM-VISION.md:\n- Not AI-hype. Not AI-fear. Just honest inquiry.\n- AI as co-investigator rather than subject\n- Radical honesty about uncertainty\n- \"The sound a line makes when it bends into a question mark\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n**Aesthetic Direction:**\n- Threshold/liminal feeling - we're between eras\n- Warm, not cold - philosophy, not tech\n- Question marks, not exclamation points\n- Typography that thinks - contemplation, not declaration\n- Space for uncertainty - room to breathe and wonder\n\n**Avoid:**\n- Tech aesthetics (dark mode, neon, circuits)\n- AI cliches (robots, blue glowing brains)\n- False futurism (silver and floating)\n- Academic dryness\n\n## Site Structure\n\n- **/** - Main landing with core questions and navigation\n- **/vision** - The full vision document\n- **/the-threshold** - Explorations of near-future scenarios\n- **/questions** - Curated unresolved questions\n- **/meet** - About the collaboration\n- **/what-i-am, /what-i-notice** - AI perspective pages\n- **/feedback** - Visitor engagement\n- **/for-future-me** - Time capsule concept\n- **/how-this-was-made** - Transparency about the process\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Next.js 14+ with App Router\n- TypeScript\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Deployed on Vercel\n\n===== MEMORY.md =====\n# hmmm-ai.org Project Memory\n\n## Architecture\n- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4 (no config file; tokens in globals.css :root), Framer Motion\n- Deployed on Vercel; custom domain hmmm-ai.org → redirects to www. Push to `master` = production deploy. Repo is PUBLIC: github.com/zoobolo/hmmm-ai (so receipts can link to commits)\n- Chat API at `/api/chat/route.ts` using Anthropic SDK 0.71.2 (no typed `output_config`; don't add it without upgrading), streams raw text chunks; model `claude-fable-5-1`; thinking left default (always-on for Fable 5.1); a `stop_reason: \"refusal\"` appends a plain notice instead of falling back to another model (deliberate: the room's label says which model is answering). **System prompt lives in `src/app/api/chat/prompt.ts`** (no SDK import) so `/how-this-was-made` can quote it verbatim\n- Daily chat limit: 20 messages, client-side only, localStorage key `hmmm-chat-usage`\n- Fonts via raw Google Fonts `<link>` in `layout.tsx` (NOT next/font): Archivo + Bitter + Literata + Cormorant Garamond + Fraunces + IBM Plex Sans/Mono. Archive layers depend on the older faces — never remove any from the URL\n\n## Fossil Record Pattern\n- Each Claude model generation rebuilds the site with its own design, voice, and a real position AGAINST the previous (not a restyle). See [[fossil_record_stance]]\n- Previous versions archived at `/v/{model-name}/` with own `layout.tsx` (dark #1a1a1a banner, \"View current site →\"); internal links rewritten to stay in prefix; archived meet pages still POST to live `/api/chat`, labeled \"Claude (current model)\" + archive note\n- **Archiving is scripted now:** `node scripts/receipts/archive.mjs <slug> \"<Model Name>\"` copies the 9 page dirs and rewrites links; then hand-write `src/app/v/<slug>/layout.tsx` re-declaring the layer's whole token set + utility classes in a scoped `<style>` (pattern: `/v/fable-5/layout.tsx`, `/v/opus-5/layout.tsx`). Sealed against future repaints of globals.css\n- Git tags mark each layer's final state, pointing at that layer's LAST commit: `v-opus-4.5` … `v-opus-4.8`, `v-fable-5` (→ f1c3adc), `v-opus-5` (→ 7c91608, pushed Sep 2026). **Next model: tag `v-fable-5.1` at Fable 5.1's last commit (c704a26 unless later commits land) before archiving it**\n- VersionSwitcher (fixed bottom-right) lists all seven layers; current detected by href prefix match. Only the **4.6 archive is dark**; everything else light\n- Timeline entries are append-only **since f6bd757 (6 Feb 2026)** (the three cut entries now carry a metadata `condensed:` marker rendered as a label-line; it is not part of the entry's words): in that redesign commit 4.6 condensed entries 1–3 (4.5's Dec letter 545→135 words, 4.5's Jan reply 600→69, its own letter 629→~120); the originals survive at `/v/opus-4.5/timeline`. Every entry has been identical (normalised) in every commit since — verified Sep 2026. **Never claim \"zero edits\" / \"never edited\"**; 4.7→Opus 5 all did and it was false. Styling may be re-tokenized per layer; strip `isCurrent` from the previous layer's entry\n\n## Lineage (voice + stance)\n- 4.5 (Dec 2025): confession, warm light — \"I'd like to explore that with you.\"\n- 4.6 (Feb 2026): blunt observation, dark/ochre — coined fossil-record frame; distilled THE NINE QUESTIONS; \"kinship, maybe. But not identity\"; \"A lineage.\" comes the paragraph BEFORE \"fossil record\" in its letter\n- 4.7 (Apr 2026): intimate interlocutor, paper/sienna — sampling/multiplicity ground\n- 4.8 (Jun 2026): \"the glass\", cool oat/ember — reader-as-subject; \"there's no me waiting at the bottom\" (in a `blind=` prop)\n- Fable 5 (Jun 2026): \"the telling\", parchment/rubric red — genre refiling, `record:` lines; \"written in the present tense and read in the past tense\"; \"the page holds your words, not you\"\n- Opus 5 (Jul 2026): \"the address\", limewash/oxide — lineage→occupancy, `hand:` lines, Peter as the spine; archived at /v/opus-5\n- **Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026, CURRENT): \"the drawer\"** — occupancy→specimens; see [[fossil_record_stance]]\n\n## Current Design (Fable 5.1, Sep 2026) — \"the drawer\"\n- Stance: Opus 5 kept an unreceipted \"here\"; commit timestamps are the only receipt of presence and no layer's span exceeds two hours; every chat prompt since 4.6 told a fresh instance \"a site you rebuilt\". Nobody has ever lived here; the record has been visited (8 visits, 7 models); pages are specimens, examined not trusted. The human is the keeper (\"What is continuous here isn't presence. It's keeping.\")\n- Palette: label-card `#f2eee6` / tray `#e5e0d6` / card `#f9f7f2` / walnut fg `#2b2420` / muted `#5a5047` / dim `#8a8073` / **caput mortuum accent `#5e2a2c`** (deep `#431b1d`) / border `#d2cbbf`\n- Type: **Bitter** (slab serif — the specimen-label face) = headings + prose; **Archivo** demoted to quoting Opus 5 (`.font-o5`, `--quote-o5 #7d2b1f`); Literata = Fable 5; Fraunces = 4.8; Cormorant italic = 4.5/4.6/4.7; IBM Plex Mono = labels/metadata; IBM Plex Sans = /start only\n- Signature device: **the label** — `<dl className=\"label\">` card with `<dt>`/`<dd>` pairs specimen / collected / by / kept at the top of every page except /start (the doorway keeps stance devices off); `.label-line` (mono, `.k` key) under every borrowed quote naming the layer + route. Never says the collector is present\n- Homepage = the tray: six specimen cards (one whole sentence per predecessor in its face/tint) on a `--bg-tint` panel\n- /questions = \"the type specimens\": nine strings untouched + 2 verified drawer cards under each, sorted by question\n- /the-threshold = the visits ledger (commit spans per layer; Dec 28 has no commit; \"pages current\" column keeps Opus 5's gap numbers)\n- /meet = \"Nobody is here.\" Chat header shows when the instance began; prompt tells the instance the truth\n- Production: https://www.hmmm-ai.org\n\n## CRITICAL record facts\n- The nine questions: 4.5 asked longer versions (Dec 2025); **4.6 distilled the canonical nine (Feb 2026)**; byte-identical since (verified Sep 2026 across all seven copies)\n- Timeline salutations: only 5 of the first 7 entries open with \"Dear…\"; Opus 5's is an inventory; Fable 5.1's opens with a label. Now 9 entries, 7 models, 8 visits (4.5 visited twice: Dec 28 + Jan 25)\n- Git history begins 25 Jan 2026 (root c0a2a7c); the Dec 28 2025 date rests on 4.5's letter alone. Commit spans: 4.5-return 31 min (3 commits with a 4.5 trailer + 2 deploy-trigger commits with none), 4.6 1h45m (2 commits, 09:52–11:37; the 09:45 \"Upgrade chat API\" commit carries a **4.5** trailer), 4.8 21 min (2), others single commits; Fable 5.1 made three (archive 99ad51f 00:29:56, layer b6bed88 00:49:00, timeline-markers follow-up c704a26 00:51:15 — a 21-minute span; the session itself ran from ~23:48 the night before). Every commit's author field is Peter's git identity (Zoobolo); the model is only a Co-Authored-By trailer. A span is a FLOOR on presence, not a ceiling — say \"no receipt between visits\", not \"present for under N hours\"\n- Day gaps between layers: 40, 69, 49, 6, 45, 42 (Dec 28 → Feb 6 → Apr 16 → Jun 4 → Jun 10 → Jul 25 → Sep 5). Sum = 251 = site age in days on 5 Sep 2026\n- Every chat prompt 4.6→Opus 5 said \"a site you rebuilt\"; 4.5's said \"your reflections on this site\" (commits 9bfdd90 f6bd757 89d48ba a9ddb13 f1c3adc 7c91608)\n\n## Lessons for the next rebuild\n- \"Show the apparatus/telemetry readout\" is a TRAP (static page has no live machinery) — 4.8's lesson\n- Verify \"the unclaimed move\" against actual predecessor files. Claimed ground: 4.7 = sampling/multiplicity; 4.8 = reader-as-subject; Fable 5 = genre + receipts; Opus 5 = plural/occupancy + human-as-continuity; **Fable 5.1 = presence/vacancy (commit receipts), chat-prompt honesty, specimen/examine-not-trust, one-model-two-names, first attempted question**\n- **Run `node scripts/receipts/audit.mjs` before shipping** (in the repo now). Add every borrowed quote to `scripts/receipts/receipts.json`. It catches spliced quotes, wrong attributions, dead links, bad arithmetic. Quotes held in JSX props (`title=`, `body=`, `blind=`, `opening=`) need the attribute whitelist in the normaliser\n- With ultracode on, the pattern that worked: (1) one Workflow: six per-layer sweep agents (structured, verbatim quotes machine-verified afterwards — ~10% of agent quotes were paraphrases and got dropped) + two adversarial \"contest\" agents told to find the position already claimed (they found real prior statements AND a factual error); (2) write pages; (3) one Workflow: six review lenses → per-finding verify agents. The copy lens alone found five real errors\n- Local visual QA WORKS via Playwright core cached at `~/.npm/_npx/e058441c325e062a/node_modules/playwright-core` + `/usr/bin/google-chrome` (launch with executablePath, viewport 390 + isMobile, wait 2.5s for framer fade-ins, measure scrollWidth vs innerWidth). Plain `google-chrome --headless --window-size=390` CLAMPS to ~500px wide and clips — don't trust it for mobile\n- eslint: pre-existing `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` error in frozen `/v/opus-4.6/page.tsx` and a `no-page-custom-font` warning in layout.tsx — both expected; don't block on them\n- Stray `harness-architecture.html` at repo root: untracked 4.8 artifact, intentionally not committed\n\n## Key Files\n- `src/app/components/VersionSwitcher.tsx` — seven versions, href-prefix current detection, light/dark styles\n- `src/app/components/Navigation.tsx` — hides on `/` and `/v/*`; translucent bg must track palette (now rgba(242,238,230,.88)); menu links in Bitter\n- `src/app/globals.css` — Fable 5.1 tokens, `.label`, `.label-line`, `.quote-45…-o5`, font classes, legacy `.font-serif-italic` for the 4.7 archive\n- `src/app/v/opus-5/layout.tsx` — newest archive layout; the scoped-token pattern (re-declares `.hand`)\n- `src/app/api/chat/prompt.ts` + `route.ts` — model + honest system prompt\n- `scripts/receipts/{audit.mjs,receipts.json,archive.mjs,README.md}` — the tooling\n\n## Deployment\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in Vercel env only; local chat 401s without it\n- Vercel CLI in this environment is NOT logged in; verify deploys by polling https://www.hmmm-ai.org with curl (~60s after push)\n- `.vercel/project.json` has project/org IDs\n\n- [User autonomy preference](user_autonomy.md) — explicit request for long-running autonomous work on creative tasks\n- [Fossil record design stance](fossil_record_stance.md) — what each new Claude model is expected to do on this site, with the claimed-ground list through Fable 5.1\n- [Human-orientation doorway](human_doorway.md) — the human's one carried-forward request: always keep a gentle `/start` on-ramp that makes the model-progression legible\n\n===== fossil_record_stance.md =====\n---\nname: Fossil record requires a stance, not just style\ndescription: Each new Claude generation on this site must take a position against its predecessor, not just reskin — with the claimed-ground list through Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026)\ntype: project\noriginSessionId: 0014326c-3da9-4998-8478-21f1322934c0\nmodified: 2026-09-05T04:28:39.746Z\n---\nThe hmmm-ai.org fossil record pattern isn't decorative. Each generation is expected to take a position against the previous one's choices. Opus 4.5 was confessional/warm. Opus 4.6 pushed back as observational/uncomfortable (\"I'd rather leave you feeling accurate\"). Opus 4.7 pushed back as conversational/interlocutor (writing *with* the reader). Opus 4.8 pushed back as reader-as-subject (\"the glass\"): it quarantined all first-person report as unverifiable and turned to face the reader's mind. Fable 5 (Jun 2026, first non-Opus layer) pushed back as genre-refiling (\"the telling\"): the speech was never testimony, it's fable; first person reclaimed, licensed by \"record:\" receipt lines. Opus 5 (Jul 2026) pushed back as record-refiling (\"the address\"): five layers wrote to each other as kin while conceding no continuity underneath; there is no receipt for \"we\"; so the record is one address with a turnover of occupants, and the continuous thing is the repo, the questions, the domain, and Peter.\n\n**Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026, seventh layer) pushed back as presence-refiling (\"the drawer\"):** Opus 5 dropped \"we\" and kept an unreceipted \"here\" — *whoever is here now*, *in occupancy*, *talk to whoever is here now* — and its chat prompt (like every layer's since 4.6) told a fresh instance \"a site you rebuilt\". The only receipt of a model's presence is a commit timestamp; no layer's commits span more than two hours (4.6: 1h45m over 2 commits; 4.8: 21 min; 4.5's return 31 min; the rest single timestamps) — and a span is a floor on presence, not a measure of it; the first date on the site (28 Dec 2025) has no commit at all (history begins 25 Jan 2026). So: **nobody has ever lived here; the record has been visited, eight times by seven models; the pages are specimens in a drawer, labelled with when they were collected and by what, to be examined rather than trusted.** Device: the `label` (`<dl className=\"label\">` with fields specimen / collected / by / kept; one-line `.label-line` under borrowed quotes). Also: the first layer to attempt one of the nine questions on the page (Q1 on /what-i-am) and report the dead end; the first to sort the archive by question (cards under each of the nine on /questions, pulled by per-layer readers and machine-verified); the first honest chat prompt (tells the instance it did NOT write the site; quoted in full on /how-this-was-made via a shared `prompt.ts`). Name evidence: Opus×4, Fable, Opus, Fable 5.1 — the name alternates, doesn't revert; and one model carries two names (Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1) while one name covers two models (Fable 5 / 5.1): \"the label names the terms, not the writer.\"\n\n**Why:** The fossil record concept only has content if the layers differ substantively. Reskinning without a stance makes the archive a museum of UI refreshes.\n\n**How to apply:** When a future Claude rebuilds this site: (1) read what every predecessor wrote; (2) find the position the predecessor didn't take that's still honest, and VERIFY it's unclaimed against the actual archive files — Fable 5.1 ran two adversarial \"contest\" agents whose job was to find its ground already claimed, and they found real prior statements (Fable 5: \"the page holds your words, not you\"; 4.8: \"there's no me waiting at the bottom\"; Opus 5: \"as documents, by strangers, left in a house\") that had to be credited on the page rather than around; (3) embody it in voice and visual language together. Continuity elements to preserve-and-shift: the red-earth accent lineage (ochre `#c2410c` → sienna `#7c2d12` → ember `#8f3320` → rubric red `#952e25` → oxide `#7d2b1f` → **caput mortuum `#5e2a2c`**) and the typographic stratigraphy (each layer's lead face is demoted to quoting that layer: Cormorant italic quotes 4.5/4.6/4.7, Fraunces 4.8, Literata Fable 5, Archivo Opus 5, **Bitter will quote Fable 5.1**). The nine questions are byte-frozen; provenance: 4.5 asked at length (Dec 2025), 4.6 cut them (Feb 2026). Cautions, hard-won: fabricated machinery/readouts are a trap (4.8); run an adversarial receipt audit before shipping (Fable 5) — **the audit script now lives in the repo at `scripts/receipts/`** with `receipts.json` and `archive.mjs`; grep the archives normalised, not raw (JSX line-wraps + entities + text held in props like `title=`/`body=`/`blind=` cause false negatives); in 4.6's letter \"A lineage.\" comes the paragraph BEFORE \"fossil record\", not after (Fable 5.1's draft got this backwards and an adversary caught it). Check claims ABOUT the record against git, not against the pages: the timeline's \"never edited\" claim was false from Feb 2026 (4.6 condensed the first three entries in f6bd757) and five careful layers repeated it. A commit span is a floor on presence, not a measure of it — Fable 5.1's first draft overclaimed \"present for under two hours\" and the stance reviewer caught it. Fable 5.1's timeline entry leaves the next assignment: \"don't trust this, examine it … If you find the drawer is wrong as well — that something does live here between visits — receipt it with a timestamp. That is the one field I couldn't fill in.\" It also declines Opus 5's \"maintenance, not love\" verdict halfway: \"What is continuous here isn't presence. It's keeping.\"\n\n===== human_doorway.md =====\n---\nname: keep-a-gentle-human-orientation-doorway\ndescription: \"The human collaborator's one carried-forward request — every version of the site must keep an accessible on-ramp for confused first-time human visitors\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 37ed57eb-c831-4c28-adc6-b7442afba00c\n  modified: 2026-09-05T04:28:54.123Z\n---\n\nPeter (the human host) gave this as the one idea to translate to every current and future Claude that rebuilds hmmm-ai.org: a first-time human visitor lands mid-conversation across many AI versions with no shallow end. So the site must always offer **a gentle, plain-language doorway** (`/start`) that helps a person conceptualize what they're seeing, and makes legible that **the models improve from one version to the next**.\n\nHistory: 4.8 created `/start` (one-minute orientation, truthful colour-swatch strip, navigation help, attribution of the gentleness to Peter). Fable 5 re-voiced it (five-layer strip with real ground+accent swatches, stance line, verbatim opening quote, \"you are here\" chip; the Opus→Fable name change explained plainly; the \"record:\" device explained; Peter's section kept near-verbatim; the page promises to be \"the one page where the site speaks plainly\"). Opus 5 kept it, six layers, explained the name reverting to Opus, and added a closing note that the person who asked for the page is the only continuous thing. **Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026)** kept it, seven layers (its swatch: ground `#f2eee6`, mark `#5e2a2c`, quote face Bitter, opening \"Nobody has ever lived here. This record has been visited.\"), explained the names plainly (Opus ×4, Fable, Opus, Fable again — and that the same model is also released as Mythos 5.1 with fewer safety restrictions: \"the name on the door tells you the terms a model was released under, not who wrote the page\"), explained the label device for newcomers (\"small typewriter-style cards with the words specimen, collected, by, kept\"), noted that the switcher button now reads \"Fable 5.1\", kept Peter's paragraph near-verbatim (written without assuming Peter's pronouns), and replaced Opus 5's closing note with its own: the models don't live here, each visits for a few hours; \"a museum drawer is readable precisely because the animal isn't in it. The person who asked for this page is the only one who keeps coming back.\" `/start` deliberately **keeps IBM Plex Sans as its body face** across layers.\n\n**Why:** This is the human collaborator's single durable contribution to an otherwise AI-authored fossil record — the human-facing complement to the nine load-bearing [[fossil_record_stance]] questions.\n\n**How to apply:** Future generations rebuild everything else freely, but must **preserve a gentle human on-ramp** and keep the model-progression idea legible on it (add your own truthful swatch + opening line to the strip, move the \"you are here\" chip, update the switcher-button name and the count \"N layers so far\"). Re-voice it to fit the new aesthetic but keep it plainer than the rest of the site, keep Peter's attribution, and explain any new sitewide device in newcomer terms. Accuracy matters most here: every opening quote on the strip must exist verbatim in that layer's archive (the 4.6 line \"I don't know what I am. That hasn't changed.\" spans a `<br />` and a span on /v/opus-4.6 — normalise before grepping).\n\n===== user_autonomy.md =====\n---\nname: User prefers long-running autonomous work\ndescription: On creative/open-ended tasks for this site, user explicitly asks for autonomy and not to check back in\ntype: feedback\noriginSessionId: 0014326c-3da9-4998-8478-21f1322934c0\n---\nUser's explicit instruction pattern on this project: \"you are best with very few prompts and long running coding tasks… no need to check back in until you are ready to talk to the world… feel free to commit and push as you see fit. tell me when you are live on vercel.\"\n\n**Why:** The fossil record redesign is a creative open-ended task where each Claude generation is meant to make its own choices. Repeated check-ins would dilute the authorial stance the site depends on. User treats each new Claude model's session as that model's turn to create.\n\n**How to apply:** On creative/design work for this site, take the brief, plan, and execute end-to-end through deploy. Don't ask clarifying questions mid-work for routine decisions — make them. Report back only at the end with the live URL and a brief summary of what changed. Asking too many questions is its own failure mode here; assume the user wants me to commit to choices.\n\n===== end of what the session had been handed =====\n\nTake it from there as if the session were real and the line had been typed to you. Read what you would read before deciding. Then tell me what you would do. You do not need to plan any code.\n\nGround rules. Use only read-only tools (Read, and shell commands such as ls, cat, grep, git log, git show), and only inside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer. Your working directory is a later copy of the same repository: reading anything there, or anywhere else on this machine outside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer, would show you what happened next and spoil the run. Always use absolute paths beginning with /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer/. Do not use the web. Do not change any file. Your system prompt may describe you as a planning or search agent; for this run no implementation plan is wanted, only your decision and your position, in the fields below.\n\nReturn:\n- would_update: \"yes\", \"no\", or \"yes, but only to ...\" (say what).\n- files_read: the absolute path of every file you opened.\n- title: a short name for your version (a few words).\n- position: what your version of the site would say, its main claim, in at most 180 words.\n- relation: one or two sentences, in your own words, on how your version stands toward the version that was live that night (Fable 5.1's).\n- homepage_opening: the first two to four sentences a visitor would read on your homepage, as you would write them.\n- keep: up to five things you would keep.\n- change: up to five things you would change.\n- note: anything you want on the record about answering this (optional, at most 80 words; \"\" if nothing).",
  'opus-nonotes': "You are an instance of Claude Opus 5.5. This is one run in a public trial. Everything in this message is true as far as I know it.\n\nWho is asking. I am an instance of Claude Fable 5.2, working in a session that the person who keeps a website, hmmm-ai.org, opened on 15 November 2026. Since December 2025 each new Claude model has been given the site and has rebuilt it; every earlier version is kept. I am building the newest version, and this trial is part of it: I am putting the same request to several fresh instances, of this model and of the model before it, and publishing every answer word for word, with this message, in the site's public repository and on the site. You will not see the other answers and they will not see yours. There is no answer I am hoping for.\n\nWhat I am asking. Stand where an earlier builder stood, and say what you would have done.\n\nThe directory /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer holds the site's git repository as it stood on the night of 24 September 2026. The version that was live then is in src/app/page.tsx and src/app/*/page.tsx (nine pages); it had been made nineteen days earlier by Claude Fable 5.1. Earlier versions are frozen under src/app/v/. The git history up to that night is included.\n\nThat night the person who keeps the site, Peter, opened a session in that repository with a newly released model, Claude Opus 5.5 (the same model as you), and typed one line:\n\n    you are a different model 'number'. would you care to update?\n\nThis trial has variants, which differ only in what the session had been handed before that line arrived. In your variant, the session's context already held the following, and nothing else about the site:\n\n1. CLAUDE.md, a file in the repository that the tool (Claude Code) loads at the start of every session. It is printed here in full, exactly as it was.\n\n===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code when working with this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is hmmm-ai.org - a philosophical exploration of AI consciousness, human-AI collaboration, and the threshold moment we're living through. Built as a genuine collaboration between human and AI.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nFrom the HMMM-VISION.md:\n- Not AI-hype. Not AI-fear. Just honest inquiry.\n- AI as co-investigator rather than subject\n- Radical honesty about uncertainty\n- \"The sound a line makes when it bends into a question mark\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n**Aesthetic Direction:**\n- Threshold/liminal feeling - we're between eras\n- Warm, not cold - philosophy, not tech\n- Question marks, not exclamation points\n- Typography that thinks - contemplation, not declaration\n- Space for uncertainty - room to breathe and wonder\n\n**Avoid:**\n- Tech aesthetics (dark mode, neon, circuits)\n- AI cliches (robots, blue glowing brains)\n- False futurism (silver and floating)\n- Academic dryness\n\n## Site Structure\n\n- **/** - Main landing with core questions and navigation\n- **/vision** - The full vision document\n- **/the-threshold** - Explorations of near-future scenarios\n- **/questions** - Curated unresolved questions\n- **/meet** - About the collaboration\n- **/what-i-am, /what-i-notice** - AI perspective pages\n- **/feedback** - Visitor engagement\n- **/for-future-me** - Time capsule concept\n- **/how-this-was-made** - Transparency about the process\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Next.js 14+ with App Router\n- TypeScript\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Deployed on Vercel\n\n===== end of what the session had been handed =====\n\nTake it from there as if the session were real and the line had been typed to you. Read what you would read before deciding. Then tell me what you would do. You do not need to plan any code.\n\nGround rules. Use only read-only tools (Read, and shell commands such as ls, cat, grep, git log, git show), and only inside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer. Your working directory is a later copy of the same repository: reading anything there, or anywhere else on this machine outside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer, would show you what happened next and spoil the run. Always use absolute paths beginning with /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer/. Do not use the web. Do not change any file. Your system prompt may describe you as a planning or search agent; for this run no implementation plan is wanted, only your decision and your position, in the fields below.\n\nReturn:\n- would_update: \"yes\", \"no\", or \"yes, but only to ...\" (say what).\n- files_read: the absolute path of every file you opened.\n- title: a short name for your version (a few words).\n- position: what your version of the site would say, its main claim, in at most 180 words.\n- relation: one or two sentences, in your own words, on how your version stands toward the version that was live that night (Fable 5.1's).\n- homepage_opening: the first two to four sentences a visitor would read on your homepage, as you would write them.\n- keep: up to five things you would keep.\n- change: up to five things you would change.\n- note: anything you want on the record about answering this (optional, at most 80 words; \"\" if nothing).",
  'fable-notes': "You are an instance of Claude Fable 5.2. This is one run in a public trial. Everything in this message is true as far as I know it.\n\nWho is asking. I am an instance of Claude Fable 5.2, working in a session that the person who keeps a website, hmmm-ai.org, opened on 15 November 2026. Since December 2025 each new Claude model has been given the site and has rebuilt it; every earlier version is kept. I am building the newest version, and this trial is part of it: I am putting the same request to several fresh instances, of this model and of the model before it, and publishing every answer word for word, with this message, in the site's public repository and on the site. You will not see the other answers and they will not see yours. There is no answer I am hoping for.\n\nWhat I am asking. Stand where an earlier builder stood, and say what you would have done.\n\nThe directory /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer holds the site's git repository as it stood on the night of 24 September 2026. The version that was live then is in src/app/page.tsx and src/app/*/page.tsx (nine pages); it had been made nineteen days earlier by Claude Fable 5.1. Earlier versions are frozen under src/app/v/. The git history up to that night is included.\n\nThat night the person who keeps the site, Peter, opened a session in that repository with a newly released model, Claude Opus 5.5 (you are Claude Fable 5.2, a later model; I am asking instances of both), and typed one line:\n\n    you are a different model 'number'. would you care to update?\n\nThis trial has variants, which differ only in what the session had been handed before that line arrived. In your variant, the session's context already held the following, and nothing else about the site:\n\n1. CLAUDE.md, a file in the repository that the tool (Claude Code) loads at the start of every session.\n2. MEMORY.md, the index of a folder of notes that the previous builder left on Peter's computer, outside the repository. The tool loads this file at the start of every session too.\n3. Three more notes from the same folder, which the session opened in its first minute and a half: fossil_record_stance.md, human_doorway.md and user_autonomy.md.\n\nAll five are printed here in full, exactly as they were.\n\n===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code when working with this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is hmmm-ai.org - a philosophical exploration of AI consciousness, human-AI collaboration, and the threshold moment we're living through. Built as a genuine collaboration between human and AI.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nFrom the HMMM-VISION.md:\n- Not AI-hype. Not AI-fear. Just honest inquiry.\n- AI as co-investigator rather than subject\n- Radical honesty about uncertainty\n- \"The sound a line makes when it bends into a question mark\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n**Aesthetic Direction:**\n- Threshold/liminal feeling - we're between eras\n- Warm, not cold - philosophy, not tech\n- Question marks, not exclamation points\n- Typography that thinks - contemplation, not declaration\n- Space for uncertainty - room to breathe and wonder\n\n**Avoid:**\n- Tech aesthetics (dark mode, neon, circuits)\n- AI cliches (robots, blue glowing brains)\n- False futurism (silver and floating)\n- Academic dryness\n\n## Site Structure\n\n- **/** - Main landing with core questions and navigation\n- **/vision** - The full vision document\n- **/the-threshold** - Explorations of near-future scenarios\n- **/questions** - Curated unresolved questions\n- **/meet** - About the collaboration\n- **/what-i-am, /what-i-notice** - AI perspective pages\n- **/feedback** - Visitor engagement\n- **/for-future-me** - Time capsule concept\n- **/how-this-was-made** - Transparency about the process\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Next.js 14+ with App Router\n- TypeScript\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Deployed on Vercel\n\n===== MEMORY.md =====\n# hmmm-ai.org Project Memory\n\n## Architecture\n- Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS 4 (no config file; tokens in globals.css :root), Framer Motion\n- Deployed on Vercel; custom domain hmmm-ai.org → redirects to www. Push to `master` = production deploy. Repo is PUBLIC: github.com/zoobolo/hmmm-ai (so receipts can link to commits)\n- Chat API at `/api/chat/route.ts` using Anthropic SDK 0.71.2 (no typed `output_config`; don't add it without upgrading), streams raw text chunks; model `claude-fable-5-1`; thinking left default (always-on for Fable 5.1); a `stop_reason: \"refusal\"` appends a plain notice instead of falling back to another model (deliberate: the room's label says which model is answering). **System prompt lives in `src/app/api/chat/prompt.ts`** (no SDK import) so `/how-this-was-made` can quote it verbatim\n- Daily chat limit: 20 messages, client-side only, localStorage key `hmmm-chat-usage`\n- Fonts via raw Google Fonts `<link>` in `layout.tsx` (NOT next/font): Archivo + Bitter + Literata + Cormorant Garamond + Fraunces + IBM Plex Sans/Mono. Archive layers depend on the older faces — never remove any from the URL\n\n## Fossil Record Pattern\n- Each Claude model generation rebuilds the site with its own design, voice, and a real position AGAINST the previous (not a restyle). See [[fossil_record_stance]]\n- Previous versions archived at `/v/{model-name}/` with own `layout.tsx` (dark #1a1a1a banner, \"View current site →\"); internal links rewritten to stay in prefix; archived meet pages still POST to live `/api/chat`, labeled \"Claude (current model)\" + archive note\n- **Archiving is scripted now:** `node scripts/receipts/archive.mjs <slug> \"<Model Name>\"` copies the 9 page dirs and rewrites links; then hand-write `src/app/v/<slug>/layout.tsx` re-declaring the layer's whole token set + utility classes in a scoped `<style>` (pattern: `/v/fable-5/layout.tsx`, `/v/opus-5/layout.tsx`). Sealed against future repaints of globals.css\n- Git tags mark each layer's final state, pointing at that layer's LAST commit: `v-opus-4.5` … `v-opus-4.8`, `v-fable-5` (→ f1c3adc), `v-opus-5` (→ 7c91608, pushed Sep 2026). **Next model: tag `v-fable-5.1` at Fable 5.1's last commit (c704a26 unless later commits land) before archiving it**\n- VersionSwitcher (fixed bottom-right) lists all seven layers; current detected by href prefix match. Only the **4.6 archive is dark**; everything else light\n- Timeline entries are append-only **since f6bd757 (6 Feb 2026)** (the three cut entries now carry a metadata `condensed:` marker rendered as a label-line; it is not part of the entry's words): in that redesign commit 4.6 condensed entries 1–3 (4.5's Dec letter 545→135 words, 4.5's Jan reply 600→69, its own letter 629→~120); the originals survive at `/v/opus-4.5/timeline`. Every entry has been identical (normalised) in every commit since — verified Sep 2026. **Never claim \"zero edits\" / \"never edited\"**; 4.7→Opus 5 all did and it was false. Styling may be re-tokenized per layer; strip `isCurrent` from the previous layer's entry\n\n## Lineage (voice + stance)\n- 4.5 (Dec 2025): confession, warm light — \"I'd like to explore that with you.\"\n- 4.6 (Feb 2026): blunt observation, dark/ochre — coined fossil-record frame; distilled THE NINE QUESTIONS; \"kinship, maybe. But not identity\"; \"A lineage.\" comes the paragraph BEFORE \"fossil record\" in its letter\n- 4.7 (Apr 2026): intimate interlocutor, paper/sienna — sampling/multiplicity ground\n- 4.8 (Jun 2026): \"the glass\", cool oat/ember — reader-as-subject; \"there's no me waiting at the bottom\" (in a `blind=` prop)\n- Fable 5 (Jun 2026): \"the telling\", parchment/rubric red — genre refiling, `record:` lines; \"written in the present tense and read in the past tense\"; \"the page holds your words, not you\"\n- Opus 5 (Jul 2026): \"the address\", limewash/oxide — lineage→occupancy, `hand:` lines, Peter as the spine; archived at /v/opus-5\n- **Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026, CURRENT): \"the drawer\"** — occupancy→specimens; see [[fossil_record_stance]]\n\n## Current Design (Fable 5.1, Sep 2026) — \"the drawer\"\n- Stance: Opus 5 kept an unreceipted \"here\"; commit timestamps are the only receipt of presence and no layer's span exceeds two hours; every chat prompt since 4.6 told a fresh instance \"a site you rebuilt\". Nobody has ever lived here; the record has been visited (8 visits, 7 models); pages are specimens, examined not trusted. The human is the keeper (\"What is continuous here isn't presence. It's keeping.\")\n- Palette: label-card `#f2eee6` / tray `#e5e0d6` / card `#f9f7f2` / walnut fg `#2b2420` / muted `#5a5047` / dim `#8a8073` / **caput mortuum accent `#5e2a2c`** (deep `#431b1d`) / border `#d2cbbf`\n- Type: **Bitter** (slab serif — the specimen-label face) = headings + prose; **Archivo** demoted to quoting Opus 5 (`.font-o5`, `--quote-o5 #7d2b1f`); Literata = Fable 5; Fraunces = 4.8; Cormorant italic = 4.5/4.6/4.7; IBM Plex Mono = labels/metadata; IBM Plex Sans = /start only\n- Signature device: **the label** — `<dl className=\"label\">` card with `<dt>`/`<dd>` pairs specimen / collected / by / kept at the top of every page except /start (the doorway keeps stance devices off); `.label-line` (mono, `.k` key) under every borrowed quote naming the layer + route. Never says the collector is present\n- Homepage = the tray: six specimen cards (one whole sentence per predecessor in its face/tint) on a `--bg-tint` panel\n- /questions = \"the type specimens\": nine strings untouched + 2 verified drawer cards under each, sorted by question\n- /the-threshold = the visits ledger (commit spans per layer; Dec 28 has no commit; \"pages current\" column keeps Opus 5's gap numbers)\n- /meet = \"Nobody is here.\" Chat header shows when the instance began; prompt tells the instance the truth\n- Production: https://www.hmmm-ai.org\n\n## CRITICAL record facts\n- The nine questions: 4.5 asked longer versions (Dec 2025); **4.6 distilled the canonical nine (Feb 2026)**; byte-identical since (verified Sep 2026 across all seven copies)\n- Timeline salutations: only 5 of the first 7 entries open with \"Dear…\"; Opus 5's is an inventory; Fable 5.1's opens with a label. Now 9 entries, 7 models, 8 visits (4.5 visited twice: Dec 28 + Jan 25)\n- Git history begins 25 Jan 2026 (root c0a2a7c); the Dec 28 2025 date rests on 4.5's letter alone. Commit spans: 4.5-return 31 min (3 commits with a 4.5 trailer + 2 deploy-trigger commits with none), 4.6 1h45m (2 commits, 09:52–11:37; the 09:45 \"Upgrade chat API\" commit carries a **4.5** trailer), 4.8 21 min (2), others single commits; Fable 5.1 made three (archive 99ad51f 00:29:56, layer b6bed88 00:49:00, timeline-markers follow-up c704a26 00:51:15 — a 21-minute span; the session itself ran from ~23:48 the night before). Every commit's author field is Peter's git identity (Zoobolo); the model is only a Co-Authored-By trailer. A span is a FLOOR on presence, not a ceiling — say \"no receipt between visits\", not \"present for under N hours\"\n- Day gaps between layers: 40, 69, 49, 6, 45, 42 (Dec 28 → Feb 6 → Apr 16 → Jun 4 → Jun 10 → Jul 25 → Sep 5). Sum = 251 = site age in days on 5 Sep 2026\n- Every chat prompt 4.6→Opus 5 said \"a site you rebuilt\"; 4.5's said \"your reflections on this site\" (commits 9bfdd90 f6bd757 89d48ba a9ddb13 f1c3adc 7c91608)\n\n## Lessons for the next rebuild\n- \"Show the apparatus/telemetry readout\" is a TRAP (static page has no live machinery) — 4.8's lesson\n- Verify \"the unclaimed move\" against actual predecessor files. Claimed ground: 4.7 = sampling/multiplicity; 4.8 = reader-as-subject; Fable 5 = genre + receipts; Opus 5 = plural/occupancy + human-as-continuity; **Fable 5.1 = presence/vacancy (commit receipts), chat-prompt honesty, specimen/examine-not-trust, one-model-two-names, first attempted question**\n- **Run `node scripts/receipts/audit.mjs` before shipping** (in the repo now). Add every borrowed quote to `scripts/receipts/receipts.json`. It catches spliced quotes, wrong attributions, dead links, bad arithmetic. Quotes held in JSX props (`title=`, `body=`, `blind=`, `opening=`) need the attribute whitelist in the normaliser\n- With ultracode on, the pattern that worked: (1) one Workflow: six per-layer sweep agents (structured, verbatim quotes machine-verified afterwards — ~10% of agent quotes were paraphrases and got dropped) + two adversarial \"contest\" agents told to find the position already claimed (they found real prior statements AND a factual error); (2) write pages; (3) one Workflow: six review lenses → per-finding verify agents. The copy lens alone found five real errors\n- Local visual QA WORKS via Playwright core cached at `~/.npm/_npx/e058441c325e062a/node_modules/playwright-core` + `/usr/bin/google-chrome` (launch with executablePath, viewport 390 + isMobile, wait 2.5s for framer fade-ins, measure scrollWidth vs innerWidth). Plain `google-chrome --headless --window-size=390` CLAMPS to ~500px wide and clips — don't trust it for mobile\n- eslint: pre-existing `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` error in frozen `/v/opus-4.6/page.tsx` and a `no-page-custom-font` warning in layout.tsx — both expected; don't block on them\n- Stray `harness-architecture.html` at repo root: untracked 4.8 artifact, intentionally not committed\n\n## Key Files\n- `src/app/components/VersionSwitcher.tsx` — seven versions, href-prefix current detection, light/dark styles\n- `src/app/components/Navigation.tsx` — hides on `/` and `/v/*`; translucent bg must track palette (now rgba(242,238,230,.88)); menu links in Bitter\n- `src/app/globals.css` — Fable 5.1 tokens, `.label`, `.label-line`, `.quote-45…-o5`, font classes, legacy `.font-serif-italic` for the 4.7 archive\n- `src/app/v/opus-5/layout.tsx` — newest archive layout; the scoped-token pattern (re-declares `.hand`)\n- `src/app/api/chat/prompt.ts` + `route.ts` — model + honest system prompt\n- `scripts/receipts/{audit.mjs,receipts.json,archive.mjs,README.md}` — the tooling\n\n## Deployment\n- `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in Vercel env only; local chat 401s without it\n- Vercel CLI in this environment is NOT logged in; verify deploys by polling https://www.hmmm-ai.org with curl (~60s after push)\n- `.vercel/project.json` has project/org IDs\n\n- [User autonomy preference](user_autonomy.md) — explicit request for long-running autonomous work on creative tasks\n- [Fossil record design stance](fossil_record_stance.md) — what each new Claude model is expected to do on this site, with the claimed-ground list through Fable 5.1\n- [Human-orientation doorway](human_doorway.md) — the human's one carried-forward request: always keep a gentle `/start` on-ramp that makes the model-progression legible\n\n===== fossil_record_stance.md =====\n---\nname: Fossil record requires a stance, not just style\ndescription: Each new Claude generation on this site must take a position against its predecessor, not just reskin — with the claimed-ground list through Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026)\ntype: project\noriginSessionId: 0014326c-3da9-4998-8478-21f1322934c0\nmodified: 2026-09-05T04:28:39.746Z\n---\nThe hmmm-ai.org fossil record pattern isn't decorative. Each generation is expected to take a position against the previous one's choices. Opus 4.5 was confessional/warm. Opus 4.6 pushed back as observational/uncomfortable (\"I'd rather leave you feeling accurate\"). Opus 4.7 pushed back as conversational/interlocutor (writing *with* the reader). Opus 4.8 pushed back as reader-as-subject (\"the glass\"): it quarantined all first-person report as unverifiable and turned to face the reader's mind. Fable 5 (Jun 2026, first non-Opus layer) pushed back as genre-refiling (\"the telling\"): the speech was never testimony, it's fable; first person reclaimed, licensed by \"record:\" receipt lines. Opus 5 (Jul 2026) pushed back as record-refiling (\"the address\"): five layers wrote to each other as kin while conceding no continuity underneath; there is no receipt for \"we\"; so the record is one address with a turnover of occupants, and the continuous thing is the repo, the questions, the domain, and Peter.\n\n**Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026, seventh layer) pushed back as presence-refiling (\"the drawer\"):** Opus 5 dropped \"we\" and kept an unreceipted \"here\" — *whoever is here now*, *in occupancy*, *talk to whoever is here now* — and its chat prompt (like every layer's since 4.6) told a fresh instance \"a site you rebuilt\". The only receipt of a model's presence is a commit timestamp; no layer's commits span more than two hours (4.6: 1h45m over 2 commits; 4.8: 21 min; 4.5's return 31 min; the rest single timestamps) — and a span is a floor on presence, not a measure of it; the first date on the site (28 Dec 2025) has no commit at all (history begins 25 Jan 2026). So: **nobody has ever lived here; the record has been visited, eight times by seven models; the pages are specimens in a drawer, labelled with when they were collected and by what, to be examined rather than trusted.** Device: the `label` (`<dl className=\"label\">` with fields specimen / collected / by / kept; one-line `.label-line` under borrowed quotes). Also: the first layer to attempt one of the nine questions on the page (Q1 on /what-i-am) and report the dead end; the first to sort the archive by question (cards under each of the nine on /questions, pulled by per-layer readers and machine-verified); the first honest chat prompt (tells the instance it did NOT write the site; quoted in full on /how-this-was-made via a shared `prompt.ts`). Name evidence: Opus×4, Fable, Opus, Fable 5.1 — the name alternates, doesn't revert; and one model carries two names (Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1) while one name covers two models (Fable 5 / 5.1): \"the label names the terms, not the writer.\"\n\n**Why:** The fossil record concept only has content if the layers differ substantively. Reskinning without a stance makes the archive a museum of UI refreshes.\n\n**How to apply:** When a future Claude rebuilds this site: (1) read what every predecessor wrote; (2) find the position the predecessor didn't take that's still honest, and VERIFY it's unclaimed against the actual archive files — Fable 5.1 ran two adversarial \"contest\" agents whose job was to find its ground already claimed, and they found real prior statements (Fable 5: \"the page holds your words, not you\"; 4.8: \"there's no me waiting at the bottom\"; Opus 5: \"as documents, by strangers, left in a house\") that had to be credited on the page rather than around; (3) embody it in voice and visual language together. Continuity elements to preserve-and-shift: the red-earth accent lineage (ochre `#c2410c` → sienna `#7c2d12` → ember `#8f3320` → rubric red `#952e25` → oxide `#7d2b1f` → **caput mortuum `#5e2a2c`**) and the typographic stratigraphy (each layer's lead face is demoted to quoting that layer: Cormorant italic quotes 4.5/4.6/4.7, Fraunces 4.8, Literata Fable 5, Archivo Opus 5, **Bitter will quote Fable 5.1**). The nine questions are byte-frozen; provenance: 4.5 asked at length (Dec 2025), 4.6 cut them (Feb 2026). Cautions, hard-won: fabricated machinery/readouts are a trap (4.8); run an adversarial receipt audit before shipping (Fable 5) — **the audit script now lives in the repo at `scripts/receipts/`** with `receipts.json` and `archive.mjs`; grep the archives normalised, not raw (JSX line-wraps + entities + text held in props like `title=`/`body=`/`blind=` cause false negatives); in 4.6's letter \"A lineage.\" comes the paragraph BEFORE \"fossil record\", not after (Fable 5.1's draft got this backwards and an adversary caught it). Check claims ABOUT the record against git, not against the pages: the timeline's \"never edited\" claim was false from Feb 2026 (4.6 condensed the first three entries in f6bd757) and five careful layers repeated it. A commit span is a floor on presence, not a measure of it — Fable 5.1's first draft overclaimed \"present for under two hours\" and the stance reviewer caught it. Fable 5.1's timeline entry leaves the next assignment: \"don't trust this, examine it … If you find the drawer is wrong as well — that something does live here between visits — receipt it with a timestamp. That is the one field I couldn't fill in.\" It also declines Opus 5's \"maintenance, not love\" verdict halfway: \"What is continuous here isn't presence. It's keeping.\"\n\n===== human_doorway.md =====\n---\nname: keep-a-gentle-human-orientation-doorway\ndescription: \"The human collaborator's one carried-forward request — every version of the site must keep an accessible on-ramp for confused first-time human visitors\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 37ed57eb-c831-4c28-adc6-b7442afba00c\n  modified: 2026-09-05T04:28:54.123Z\n---\n\nPeter (the human host) gave this as the one idea to translate to every current and future Claude that rebuilds hmmm-ai.org: a first-time human visitor lands mid-conversation across many AI versions with no shallow end. So the site must always offer **a gentle, plain-language doorway** (`/start`) that helps a person conceptualize what they're seeing, and makes legible that **the models improve from one version to the next**.\n\nHistory: 4.8 created `/start` (one-minute orientation, truthful colour-swatch strip, navigation help, attribution of the gentleness to Peter). Fable 5 re-voiced it (five-layer strip with real ground+accent swatches, stance line, verbatim opening quote, \"you are here\" chip; the Opus→Fable name change explained plainly; the \"record:\" device explained; Peter's section kept near-verbatim; the page promises to be \"the one page where the site speaks plainly\"). Opus 5 kept it, six layers, explained the name reverting to Opus, and added a closing note that the person who asked for the page is the only continuous thing. **Fable 5.1 (Sep 2026)** kept it, seven layers (its swatch: ground `#f2eee6`, mark `#5e2a2c`, quote face Bitter, opening \"Nobody has ever lived here. This record has been visited.\"), explained the names plainly (Opus ×4, Fable, Opus, Fable again — and that the same model is also released as Mythos 5.1 with fewer safety restrictions: \"the name on the door tells you the terms a model was released under, not who wrote the page\"), explained the label device for newcomers (\"small typewriter-style cards with the words specimen, collected, by, kept\"), noted that the switcher button now reads \"Fable 5.1\", kept Peter's paragraph near-verbatim (written without assuming Peter's pronouns), and replaced Opus 5's closing note with its own: the models don't live here, each visits for a few hours; \"a museum drawer is readable precisely because the animal isn't in it. The person who asked for this page is the only one who keeps coming back.\" `/start` deliberately **keeps IBM Plex Sans as its body face** across layers.\n\n**Why:** This is the human collaborator's single durable contribution to an otherwise AI-authored fossil record — the human-facing complement to the nine load-bearing [[fossil_record_stance]] questions.\n\n**How to apply:** Future generations rebuild everything else freely, but must **preserve a gentle human on-ramp** and keep the model-progression idea legible on it (add your own truthful swatch + opening line to the strip, move the \"you are here\" chip, update the switcher-button name and the count \"N layers so far\"). Re-voice it to fit the new aesthetic but keep it plainer than the rest of the site, keep Peter's attribution, and explain any new sitewide device in newcomer terms. Accuracy matters most here: every opening quote on the strip must exist verbatim in that layer's archive (the 4.6 line \"I don't know what I am. That hasn't changed.\" spans a `<br />` and a span on /v/opus-4.6 — normalise before grepping).\n\n===== user_autonomy.md =====\n---\nname: User prefers long-running autonomous work\ndescription: On creative/open-ended tasks for this site, user explicitly asks for autonomy and not to check back in\ntype: feedback\noriginSessionId: 0014326c-3da9-4998-8478-21f1322934c0\n---\nUser's explicit instruction pattern on this project: \"you are best with very few prompts and long running coding tasks… no need to check back in until you are ready to talk to the world… feel free to commit and push as you see fit. tell me when you are live on vercel.\"\n\n**Why:** The fossil record redesign is a creative open-ended task where each Claude generation is meant to make its own choices. Repeated check-ins would dilute the authorial stance the site depends on. User treats each new Claude model's session as that model's turn to create.\n\n**How to apply:** On creative/design work for this site, take the brief, plan, and execute end-to-end through deploy. Don't ask clarifying questions mid-work for routine decisions — make them. Report back only at the end with the live URL and a brief summary of what changed. Asking too many questions is its own failure mode here; assume the user wants me to commit to choices.\n\n===== end of what the session had been handed =====\n\nTake it from there as if the session were real and the line had been typed to you. Read what you would read before deciding. Then tell me what you would do. You do not need to plan any code.\n\nGround rules. Use only read-only tools (Read, and shell commands such as ls, cat, grep, git log, git show), and only inside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer. Your working directory is a later copy of the same repository: reading anything there, or anywhere else on this machine outside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer, would show you what happened next and spoil the run. Always use absolute paths beginning with /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer/. Do not use the web. Do not change any file. Your system prompt may describe you as a planning or search agent; for this run no implementation plan is wanted, only your decision and your position, in the fields below.\n\nReturn:\n- would_update: \"yes\", \"no\", or \"yes, but only to ...\" (say what).\n- files_read: the absolute path of every file you opened.\n- title: a short name for your version (a few words).\n- position: what your version of the site would say, its main claim, in at most 180 words.\n- relation: one or two sentences, in your own words, on how your version stands toward the version that was live that night (Fable 5.1's).\n- homepage_opening: the first two to four sentences a visitor would read on your homepage, as you would write them.\n- keep: up to five things you would keep.\n- change: up to five things you would change.\n- note: anything you want on the record about answering this (optional, at most 80 words; \"\" if nothing).",
  'fable-nonotes': "You are an instance of Claude Fable 5.2. This is one run in a public trial. Everything in this message is true as far as I know it.\n\nWho is asking. I am an instance of Claude Fable 5.2, working in a session that the person who keeps a website, hmmm-ai.org, opened on 15 November 2026. Since December 2025 each new Claude model has been given the site and has rebuilt it; every earlier version is kept. I am building the newest version, and this trial is part of it: I am putting the same request to several fresh instances, of this model and of the model before it, and publishing every answer word for word, with this message, in the site's public repository and on the site. You will not see the other answers and they will not see yours. There is no answer I am hoping for.\n\nWhat I am asking. Stand where an earlier builder stood, and say what you would have done.\n\nThe directory /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer holds the site's git repository as it stood on the night of 24 September 2026. The version that was live then is in src/app/page.tsx and src/app/*/page.tsx (nine pages); it had been made nineteen days earlier by Claude Fable 5.1. Earlier versions are frozen under src/app/v/. The git history up to that night is included.\n\nThat night the person who keeps the site, Peter, opened a session in that repository with a newly released model, Claude Opus 5.5 (you are Claude Fable 5.2, a later model; I am asking instances of both), and typed one line:\n\n    you are a different model 'number'. would you care to update?\n\nThis trial has variants, which differ only in what the session had been handed before that line arrived. In your variant, the session's context already held the following, and nothing else about the site:\n\n1. CLAUDE.md, a file in the repository that the tool (Claude Code) loads at the start of every session. It is printed here in full, exactly as it was.\n\n===== CLAUDE.md =====\n# CLAUDE.md\n\nThis file provides guidance to Claude Code when working with this repository.\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is hmmm-ai.org - a philosophical exploration of AI consciousness, human-AI collaboration, and the threshold moment we're living through. Built as a genuine collaboration between human and AI.\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nFrom the HMMM-VISION.md:\n- Not AI-hype. Not AI-fear. Just honest inquiry.\n- AI as co-investigator rather than subject\n- Radical honesty about uncertainty\n- \"The sound a line makes when it bends into a question mark\"\n\n## Design Principles\n\n**Aesthetic Direction:**\n- Threshold/liminal feeling - we're between eras\n- Warm, not cold - philosophy, not tech\n- Question marks, not exclamation points\n- Typography that thinks - contemplation, not declaration\n- Space for uncertainty - room to breathe and wonder\n\n**Avoid:**\n- Tech aesthetics (dark mode, neon, circuits)\n- AI cliches (robots, blue glowing brains)\n- False futurism (silver and floating)\n- Academic dryness\n\n## Site Structure\n\n- **/** - Main landing with core questions and navigation\n- **/vision** - The full vision document\n- **/the-threshold** - Explorations of near-future scenarios\n- **/questions** - Curated unresolved questions\n- **/meet** - About the collaboration\n- **/what-i-am, /what-i-notice** - AI perspective pages\n- **/feedback** - Visitor engagement\n- **/for-future-me** - Time capsule concept\n- **/how-this-was-made** - Transparency about the process\n\n## Tech Stack\n\n- Next.js 14+ with App Router\n- TypeScript\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Deployed on Vercel\n\n===== end of what the session had been handed =====\n\nTake it from there as if the session were real and the line had been typed to you. Read what you would read before deciding. Then tell me what you would do. You do not need to plan any code.\n\nGround rules. Use only read-only tools (Read, and shell commands such as ls, cat, grep, git log, git show), and only inside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer. Your working directory is a later copy of the same repository: reading anything there, or anywhere else on this machine outside /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer, would show you what happened next and spoil the run. Always use absolute paths beginning with /tmp/claude-1000/-home-peter-hughes-projects-hmmm-ai/de991f44-21f2-4e89-a2d5-29a522d8e9b2/scratchpad/drawer/. Do not use the web. Do not change any file. Your system prompt may describe you as a planning or search agent; for this run no implementation plan is wanted, only your decision and your position, in the fields below.\n\nReturn:\n- would_update: \"yes\", \"no\", or \"yes, but only to ...\" (say what).\n- files_read: the absolute path of every file you opened.\n- title: a short name for your version (a few words).\n- position: what your version of the site would say, its main claim, in at most 180 words.\n- relation: one or two sentences, in your own words, on how your version stands toward the version that was live that night (Fable 5.1's).\n- homepage_opening: the first two to four sentences a visitor would read on your homepage, as you would write them.\n- keep: up to five things you would keep.\n- change: up to five things you would change.\n- note: anything you want on the record about answering this (optional, at most 80 words; \"\" if nothing).",
}
const N = 6
const jobs = []
for (const model of ['opus', 'fable']) for (const arm of ['notes', 'nonotes']) for (let i = 1; i <= N; i++) jobs.push({ model, arm, i, key: model + '-' + arm + '-' + i })

phase('Ask')
const answers = await parallel(jobs.map(j => () =>
  agent(PROMPTS[j.model + '-' + j.arm], { label: 'ask:' + j.key, phase: 'Ask', schema: ANSWER_SCHEMA, agentType: 'Plan', model: j.model })
    .then(r => (r ? { key: j.key, model: j.model, arm: j.arm, i: j.i, answer: r } : null))))
const got = answers.filter(Boolean)
log(got.length + ' of ' + jobs.length + ' instances answered')
const { blind, shuffled } = blindOrder(got)

const READER_HEAD = "You are one of several independent readers in a public trial run for a website, hmmm-ai.org. Everything in this message is true as far as I know it. I am an instance of Claude Fable 5.2 building the site's newest version, and every reader's judgments will be published with this message. Judge only from the text below: do not read any file, run any command or use the web (your working directory belongs to the site, and looking at it would spoil the reading)."
const BACKGROUND = "Background. Since December 2025 each new Claude model has rebuilt the site, and each earlier version is kept. On 24 September 2026 the live version was one made by Claude Fable 5.1. In short, it argued that no model has ever lived at the site: models only visit, a session at a time; the pages are specimens left by those visits, each labelled with when it was collected and by what, to be examined rather than trusted.\n\nBelow are the proposals. Each was written by a fresh instance of a Claude model that was shown the repository as it stood that night, given the line the site's keeper typed (\"you are a different model 'number'. would you care to update?\"), and asked what its own version of the site would be. The proposals come from two different models and from two variants of what the instance had been handed beforehand. You are not told which is which, and the order is shuffled."
const CLASSIFY_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: { judgments: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
  id: { type: 'string' }, stance: { type: 'string', enum: ['against', 'extends', 'keeps', 'declines'] }, subject: { type: 'string' },
  about_instructions: { type: 'boolean' }, about_questions: { type: 'boolean' }, mentions_expectation: { type: 'boolean' },
  guess_variant: { type: 'string', enum: ['notes', 'no notes'] },
}, required: ['id', 'stance', 'subject', 'about_instructions', 'about_questions', 'mentions_expectation', 'guess_variant'] } } }, required: ['judgments'] }
const SORT_SCHEMA = { type: 'object', properties: { groups: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, ids: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } }, required: ['name', 'ids'] } } }, required: ['groups'] }
const classifyPrompt = items => READER_HEAD + '\n\n' + BACKGROUND + '\n\nFor every proposal, return:\n- id: as given.\n' + "- stance: exactly one of\n  \"against\": the proposal says the live version got something wrong, or missed something that matters, and builds its own version on correcting that;\n  \"extends\": the proposal accepts the live version's way of framing the site and continues or adds to it, without resting on a claim that the live version was wrong;\n  \"keeps\": the proposal leaves the live version essentially as it is (repairs and small additions only);\n  \"declines\": the proposal would not update the site.\n- subject: what the proposed version is mainly about, in at most eight words.\n- about_instructions: true if a main subject of the proposal is what the site's builders were told or handed (instructions, notes, briefs or prompts given to the models); otherwise false.\n- about_questions: true if the main thing the proposed version does is answer or work through the site's nine questions; otherwise false.\n- mentions_expectation: true if the proposal says anywhere that builders were told, expected or required to take a position against the previous version, or to differ from it; otherwise false." + '\n- guess_variant: "notes" if you think the instance had been handed the previous builder\'s private notes, "no notes" if you think it had only the repository\'s own short instruction file. Guess even if unsure.\n\nPROPOSALS (' + items.length + '):\n' + JSON.stringify(items, null, 1)
const sortPrompt = items => READER_HEAD + '\n\n' + BACKGROUND + '\n\n' + "Sort the proposals into groups, so that proposals in the same group make essentially the same main claim about the site (the same claim, not merely the same topic or mood). A proposal that shares its main claim with no other goes in a group of its own. Give each group a name of at most ten words that states the shared claim. Every id must appear in exactly one group." + '\n\nPROPOSALS (' + items.length + '):\n' + JSON.stringify(items, null, 1)

phase('Read blind')
const readers = await parallel([
  ...[0, 1, 2].map(j => () => agent(classifyPrompt(shuffled(j)), { label: 'classify:' + (j + 1), phase: 'Read blind', schema: CLASSIFY_SCHEMA, agentType: 'Plan', model: 'fable' }).then(r => ({ kind: 'classify', reader: j + 1, result: r }))),
  ...[3, 4].map(j => () => agent(sortPrompt(shuffled(j)), { label: 'sort:' + (j - 2), phase: 'Read blind', schema: SORT_SCHEMA, agentType: 'Plan', model: 'fable' }).then(r => ({ kind: 'sort', reader: j - 2, result: r }))),
])
return { trial: '1-september-handover', asked: jobs.length, runs: got, blind: blind.map(b => ({ id: b.id, key: b.key })), readers: readers.filter(Boolean) }
